An argument's register interpolation occurs once at invocation. Repeated use
inserts that value without reinterpreting it. Disabled branches do no body work.
-- input.roff --
.nr X 0 1
.de REPEAT
\\$1 \\$1
.if 0 \\n+[X]
.if 1 \\$2
..
.REPEAT \n+[X] literal
\n[X]
-- expected.txt --
groff.TokenText "1 1"
groff.TokenText "literal"
groff.TokenText "1"
register X=1
-- parsed.txt --
*groff.TokenRequestNr ".nr X 0 1"
*groff.TokenMacroDefinition ".de REPEAT\n\\\\$1 \\\\$1\n.if 0 \\\\n+[X]\n.if 1 \\\\$2\n.."
*groff.TokenUnknownControl ".REPEAT \\n+[X] literal"
groff.TokenText "\\n[X]"
